-- ccc7-s195-notification.l4 -- sections 195 (annual reports), 196 (written notification of an interception under an authorization) and 196.1 (written notice of an interception under section 184.4)
-- of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part VI.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against it.
-- What these sections mean to the person in the seat: sections 196 and 196.1 are the person's right to be told, in writing and within 90 days (or the longer period a judge allows, up to three years at a time), that their private
-- communications were intercepted. Section 195 (the annual reports to Parliament and by each province) addresses only officials: it is encoded for what it decides (what the reports must contain, when they must be laid before
-- Parliament) and has no question in the seat layer. Section 195 is not in the list of "machinery" in the brief's reason 2, so it is encoded, not inert; the lead may downgrade it.
-- Periods keep the text's units: 90 days is a number of days after a date; the longer periods are a Length of time (years, months, days).

§ `Section 195 -- Annual report`

DECLARE `s 195(1) matter the report relates to` IS ONE OF
    `s 195(1)(a) authorizations for which the Minister and agents specially designated by the Minister for the purposes of section 185 applied, and the interceptions made under them in the preceding year`
    `s 195(1)(b) authorizations given under section 188 for which peace officers specially designated by the Minister applied, and the interceptions made under them in the preceding year`
    `s 195(1)(c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the preceding year`
    `s 195(1) another matter`

-- 195(1): "The Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness shall, as soon as possible after the end of each year, prepare a report relating to (a) authorizations for which that Minister and agents specially designated in writing by that Minister
-- for the purposes of section 185 applied and the interceptions made under those authorizations in the immediately preceding year; (b) authorizations given under section 188 for which peace officers specially designated by that Minister for the purposes
-- of that section applied and the interceptions made under those authorizations in the immediately preceding year; and (c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the immediately preceding year if the interceptions relate to an offence for which
-- proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General of Canada."
-- src:4028 | Annual report
-- src:4029 | 195 (1) The Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness shall, as soon as possible after the end of each year, prepare a report relating to
-- src:4030 | (a) authorizations for which that Minister and agents specially designated in writing by that Minister for the purposes of section 185 applied and the interceptions made under those authorizations in the immediately preceding year;
-- src:4031 | (b) authorizations given under section 188 for which peace officers specially designated by that Minister for the purposes of that section applied and the interceptions made under those authorizations in the immediately preceding year; and
-- src:4032 | (c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the immediately preceding year if the interceptions relate to an offence for which proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 195(1) (src:4028-4032)
GIVEN `a year has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 195(1) matter the report relates to`
      `the interceptions relate to an offence for which proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(1) the Minister is bound to prepare a report relating to the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a year has ended`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as possible after the end of each year"
        IF matter EQUALS `s 195(1) another matter`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "prepare a report relating to" three matters; the text does not say that no other matter is covered
        IF (matter EQUALS `s 195(1)(c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the preceding year`) AND (NOT `the interceptions relate to an offence for which proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General of Canada`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the interceptions relate to an offence for which proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General of Canada"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 195(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 195(1) prepares the annual report`

-- src:4028 | Annual report
-- src:4029 | 195 (1) The Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness shall, as soon as possible after the end of each year, prepare a report relating to
-- src:4030 | (a) authorizations for which that Minister and agents specially designated in writing by that Minister for the purposes of section 185 applied and the interceptions made under those authorizations in the immediately preceding year;
-- src:4031 | (b) authorizations given under section 188 for which peace officers specially designated by that Minister for the purposes of that section applied and the interceptions made under those authorizations in the immediately preceding year; and
-- src:4032 | (c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the immediately preceding year if the interceptions relate to an offence for which proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 195(1) (src:4028-4032)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 183 party under Part VI` `s 195(1) act`
`s 195(1) the duty to prepare the annual report as a rule` MEANS
    PARTY `s 183 the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`
    MUST `s 195(1) prepares the annual report`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 183 the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` BECAUSE "s 195(1): the report relating to the preceding year was not prepared as soon as possible after the end of the year"

DECLARE `s 195(2) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 195(2)(a) the number of applications made for authorizations`
    `s 195(2)(b) the number of applications made for renewal of authorizations`
    `s 195(2)(c) the numbers of those applications that were granted, refused, and granted subject to terms and conditions`
    `s 195(2)(d) the number of persons identified in an authorization against whom proceedings were commenced at the instance of the Attorney General of Canada, by kind of offence`
    `s 195(2)(e) the number of persons not identified in an authorization against whom proceedings were commenced, by kind of offence, whose offence became known as a result of an interception`
    `s 195(2)(f) the average period for which authorizations were given and renewals granted`
    `s 195(2)(g) the number of authorizations valid for more than sixty, one hundred and twenty, one hundred and eighty and two hundred and forty days`
    `s 195(2)(h) the number of notifications given pursuant to section 196`
    `s 195(2)(i) the offences in respect of which authorizations were given, with the number for each`
    `s 195(2)(j) a description of all classes of places specified in authorizations and the number for each class`
    `s 195(2)(k) a general description of the methods of interception involved in each interception`
    `s 195(2)(l) the number of persons arrested whose identity became known as a result of an interception`
    `s 195(2)(m) the number of criminal proceedings in which intercepted communications were adduced in evidence and the number that resulted in a conviction`
    `s 195(2)(n) the number of criminal investigations in which information was used although the communication was not adduced in evidence`
    `s 195(2) an item that is none of those`

-- 195(2): "The report shall, in relation to the authorizations and interceptions referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b), set out (a) the number of applications made for authorizations; ... (n) the number of criminal investigations in which information obtained
-- as a result of the interception of a private communication under an authorization was used although the private communication was not adduced in evidence in criminal proceedings commenced at the instance of the Attorney General of Canada as a result of the investigations."
-- The list of items is not closed: an item it does not name is NOT COVERED. Paragraphs (d) and (e) each have three sub-paragraphs (i) to (iii), which are the kinds of offence by which the numbers are broken down.
-- src:4033 | Information respecting authorizations — sections 185 and 188
-- src:4034 | (2) The report shall, in relation to the authorizations and interceptions referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b), set out
-- src:4035 | (a) the number of applications made for authorizations;
-- src:4036 | (b) the number of applications made for renewal of authorizations;
-- src:4037 | (c) the number of applications referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) that were granted, the number of those applications that were refused and the number of applications referred to in paragraph (a) that were granted subject to terms and conditions;
-- src:4038 | (d) the number of persons identified in an authorization against whom proceedings were commenced at the instance of the Attorney General of Canada in respect of
-- src:4039 | (i) an offence specified in the authorization,
-- src:4040 | (ii) an offence other than an offence specified in the authorization but in respect of which an authorization may be given, and
-- src:4041 | (iii) an offence in respect of which an authorization may not be given;
-- src:4042 | (e) the number of persons not identified in an authorization against whom proceedings were commenced at the instance of the Attorney General of Canada in respect of
-- src:4043 | (i) an offence specified in such an authorization,
-- src:4044 | (ii) an offence other than an offence specified in such an authorization but in respect of which an authorization may be given, and
-- src:4045 | (iii) an offence other than an offence specified in such an authorization and for which no such authorization may be given,
-- src:4046 | and whose commission or alleged commission of the offence became known to a peace officer as a result of an interception of a private communication under an authorization;
-- src:4047 | (f) the average period for which authorizations were given and for which renewals thereof were granted;
-- src:4048 | (g) the number of authorizations that, by virtue of one or more renewals thereof, were valid for more than sixty days, for more than one hundred and twenty days, for more than one hundred and eighty days and for more than two hundred and forty days;
-- src:4049 | (h) the number of notifications given pursuant to section 196;
-- src:4050 | (i) the offences in respect of which authorizations were given, specifying the number of authorizations given in respect of each of those offences;
-- src:4051 | (j) a description of all classes of places specified in authorizations and the number of authorizations in which each of those classes of places was specified;
-- src:4052 | (k) a general description of the methods of interception involved in each interception under an authorization;
-- src:4053 | (l) the number of persons arrested whose identity became known to a peace officer as a result of an interception under an authorization;
-- src:4054 | (m) the number of criminal proceedings commenced at the instance of the Attorney General of Canada in which private communications obtained by interception under an authorization were adduced in evidence and the number of those proceedings that resulted in a conviction; and
-- src:4055 | (n) the number of criminal investigations in which information obtained as a result of the interception of a private communication under an authorization was used although the private communication was not adduced in evidence in criminal proceedings commenced at the instance of the Attorney General of Canada as a result of the investigations.
@ref Criminal Code s 195(2) (src:4033-4055)
GIVEN item IS A `s 195(2) item of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(2) the report must set out the item` MEANS
    IF item EQUALS `s 195(2) an item that is none of those`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists what the report shall set out; it does not say that it shall set out nothing else
    ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 195(2.1) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 195(2.1)(a) the number of interceptions made`
    `s 195(2.1)(b) the number of parties to each intercepted private communication against whom proceedings were commenced`
    `s 195(2.1)(c) the number of persons who were not parties to an intercepted private communication but whose offence became known as a result, and against whom proceedings were commenced`
    `s 195(2.1)(d) the number of notifications given under section 196.1`
    `s 195(2.1)(e) the offences in respect of which interceptions were made and any other offences for which proceedings were commenced, with the number of interceptions for each`
    `s 195(2.1)(f) a general description of the methods of interception used for each interception`
    `s 195(2.1)(g) the number of persons arrested whose identity became known to a police officer as a result of an interception`
    `s 195(2.1)(h) the number of criminal proceedings commenced in which intercepted communications were adduced in evidence and the number that resulted in a conviction`
    `s 195(2.1)(i) the number of criminal investigations in which information was used even though the communication was not adduced in evidence`
    `s 195(2.1)(j) the duration of each interception and the aggregate duration of all the interceptions related to the investigation of the offence`
    `s 195(2.1) an item that is none of those`

-- 195(2.1): "The report shall, in relation to the interceptions referred to in paragraph (1)(c), set out (a) the number of interceptions made; ... (j) the duration of each interception and the aggregate duration of all the interceptions related to the investigation of
-- the offence that the police officer sought to prevent in intercepting the private communication."
-- src:4056 | Information respecting interceptions — section 184.4
-- src:4057 | (2.1) The report shall, in relation to the interceptions referred to in paragraph (1)(c), set out
-- src:4058 | (a) the number of interceptions made;
-- src:4059 | (b) the number of parties to each intercepted private communication against whom proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence that the police officer sought to prevent in intercepting the private communication or in respect of any other offence that was detected as a result of the interception;
-- src:4060 | (c) the number of persons who were not parties to an intercepted private communication but whose commission or alleged commission of an offence became known to a police officer as a result of the interception of a private communication, and against whom proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence that the police officer sought to prevent in intercepting the private communication or in respect of any other offence that was detected as a result of the interception;
-- src:4061 | (d) the number of notifications given under section 196.1;
-- src:4062 | (e) the offences in respect of which interceptions were made and any other offences for which proceedings were commenced as a result of an interception, as well as the number of interceptions made with respect to each offence;
-- src:4063 | (f) a general description of the methods of interception used for each interception;
-- src:4064 | (g) the number of persons arrested whose identity became known to a police officer as a result of an interception;
-- src:4065 | (h) the number of criminal proceedings commenced in which private communications obtained by interception were adduced in evidence and the number of those proceedings that resulted in a conviction;
-- src:4066 | (i) the number of criminal investigations in which information obtained as a result of the interception of a private communication was used even though the private communication was not adduced in evidence in criminal proceedings commenced as a result of the investigations; and
-- src:4067 | (j) the duration of each interception and the aggregate duration of all the interceptions related to the investigation of the offence that the police officer sought to prevent in intercepting the private communication.
@ref Criminal Code s 195(2.1) (src:4056-4067)
GIVEN item IS A `s 195(2.1) item of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` MEANS
    IF item EQUALS `s 195(2.1) an item that is none of those`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists what the report shall set out; it does not say that it shall set out nothing else
    ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 195(3) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 195(3)(a) the number of prosecutions commenced against officers or servants of Her Majesty in right of Canada or members of the Canadian Forces for offences under section 184 or 193`
    `s 195(3)(b) a general assessment of the importance of interception of private communications for the investigation, detection, prevention and prosecution of offences in Canada`
    `s 195(3) an item that is none of those`

-- 195(3): "The report shall, in addition to the information referred to in subsections (2) and (2.1), set out (a) the number of prosecutions commenced against officers or servants of Her Majesty in right of Canada or members of the Canadian Forces for offences
-- under section 184 or 193; and (b) a general assessment of the importance of interception of private communications for the investigation, detection, prevention and prosecution of offences in Canada."
-- src:4068 | Other information
-- src:4069 | (3) The report shall, in addition to the information referred to in subsections (2) and (2.1), set out
-- src:4070 | (a) the number of prosecutions commenced against officers or servants of Her Majesty in right of Canada or members of the Canadian Forces for offences under section 184 or 193; and
-- src:4071 | (b) a general assessment of the importance of interception of private communications for the investigation, detection, prevention and prosecution of offences in Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 195(3) (src:4068-4071)
GIVEN item IS A `s 195(3) item of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(3) the report must set out the item` MEANS
    IF item EQUALS `s 195(3) an item that is none of those`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists what the report shall set out; it does not say that it shall set out nothing else
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 195(4): "The Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness shall cause a copy of each report prepared by him under subsection (1) to be laid before Parliament forthwith on completion thereof, or if Parliament is not then sitting, on any of the first
-- fifteen days next thereafter that Parliament is sitting." The count is of days on which Parliament sits: the first sitting day after completion is day 1.
-- src:4072 | Report to be laid before Parliament
-- src:4073 | (4) The Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness shall cause a copy of each report prepared by him under subsection (1) to be laid before Parliament forthwith on completion thereof, or if Parliament is not then sitting, on any of the first fifteen days next thereafter that Parliament is sitting.
@ref Criminal Code s 195(4) (src:4072-4073)
GIVEN `Parliament was sitting when the report was completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report was laid before Parliament forthwith on completion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report was laid on the nth day on which Parliament sat after completion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(4) the report was laid before Parliament in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Parliament was sitting when the report was completed`
        THEN IF `the report was laid before Parliament forthwith on completion`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to be laid before Parliament forthwith on completion thereof"
        IF (`the report was laid on the nth day on which Parliament sat after completion` AT LEAST 1) AND (`the report was laid on the nth day on which Parliament sat after completion` AT MOST 15)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or if Parliament is not then sitting, on any of the first fifteen days next thereafter that Parliament is sitting"

DECLARE `s 195(5) matter the report relates to` IS ONE OF
    `s 195(5)(a) authorizations for which the Attorney General and agents specially designated by the Attorney General for the purposes of section 185 applied, and the interceptions made under them in the preceding year`
    `s 195(5)(b) authorizations given under section 188 for which peace officers specially designated by the Attorney General applied, and the interceptions made under them in the preceding year`
    `s 195(5)(c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the preceding year`
    `s 195(5) another matter`

-- 195(5): "The Attorney General of each province shall, as soon as possible after the end of each year, prepare and publish or otherwise make available to the public a report relating to (a) authorizations for which the Attorney General and agents specially
-- designated in writing by the Attorney General for the purposes of section 185 applied ...; (b) authorizations given under section 188 for which peace officers specially designated by the Attorney General ... applied ...; and (c) interceptions made under
-- section 184.4 in the immediately preceding year, if the interceptions relate to an offence not referred to in paragraph (1)(c). The report must set out, with any modifications that the circumstances require, the information described in subsections (2) to (3)."
-- src:4074 | Report by Attorneys General
-- src:4075 | (5) The Attorney General of each province shall, as soon as possible after the end of each year, prepare and publish or otherwise make available to the public a report relating to
-- src:4076 | (a) authorizations for which the Attorney General and agents specially designated in writing by the Attorney General for the purposes of section 185 applied and to the interceptions made under those authorizations in the immediately preceding year;
-- src:4077 | (b) authorizations given under section 188 for which peace officers specially designated by the Attorney General for the purposes of that section applied and to the interceptions made under those authorizations in the immediately preceding year; and
-- src:4078 | (c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the immediately preceding year, if the interceptions relate to an offence not referred to in paragraph (1)(c).
-- src:4079 | The report must set out, with any modifications that the circumstances require, the information described in subsections (2) to (3).
@ref Criminal Code s 195(5) (src:4074-4079)
GIVEN `a year has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 195(5) matter the report relates to`
      `the interceptions relate to an offence not referred to in paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 195(5) the Attorney General of each province is bound to prepare and publish a report relating to the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a year has ended`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as possible after the end of each year"
        IF matter EQUALS `s 195(5) another matter`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "prepare and publish or otherwise make available to the public a report relating to" three matters; the text does not say that no other matter is covered
        IF (matter EQUALS `s 195(5)(c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the preceding year`) AND (NOT `the interceptions relate to an offence not referred to in paragraph (1)(c)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the interceptions relate to an offence not referred to in paragraph (1)(c)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 196 -- Written notification to be given`

-- A period measured from a date, in the text's units: a number of days (90), or a Length of time (years, months, days). `add years` and `add months` clamp the day of the month (daydate): 31 January plus one month is 28 or 29 February.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      period IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 196(1) the day after a period that begins on the day` MEANS
    (`add months` (`add years` day (period's years)) (period's months)) PLUS (period's days)

-- 196(2): "The running of the 90 days referred to in subsection (1), or of any other period fixed pursuant to subsection 185(3) or subsection (3) of this section, is suspended until any application made by the Attorney General or the Minister to a judge of a superior
-- court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 for an extension or a subsequent extension of the period for which the authorization was given or renewed has been heard and disposed of."
-- The days of suspension are the days from the day the application is made until the day it is disposed of: that many days are not counted.
-- src:4082 | Extension of period for notification
-- src:4083 | (2) The running of the 90 days referred to in subsection (1), or of any other period fixed pursuant to subsection 185(3) or subsection (3) of this section, is suspended until any application made by the Attorney General or the Minister to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 for an extension or a subsequent extension of the period for which the authorization was given or renewed has been heard and disposed of.
@ref Criminal Code s 196(2) (src:4082-4083)
GIVEN `the day the application for an extension was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the application was heard and disposed of` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 196(2) the number of days the running of the period is suspended` MEANS
    IF Day `the day the application was heard and disposed of` AT LEAST Day `the day the application for an extension was made`
    THEN Day `the day the application was heard and disposed of` MINUS Day `the day the application for an extension was made`
    ELSE 0

-- 196(1): "The Attorney General of the province in which an application under subsection 185(1) was made or the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness if the application was made by or on behalf of that Minister shall, within 90 days after
-- the period for which the authorization was given or renewed or within such other period as is fixed pursuant to subsection 185(3) or subsection (3) of this section, notify in writing the person who was the object of the interception pursuant to the
-- authorization and shall, in a manner prescribed by regulations made by the Governor in Council, certify to the court that gave the authorization that the person has been so notified."
-- The last day for the notice: the day the period ended plus 90 days, or plus the other period fixed, plus the days the running was suspended by subsection (2).
-- src:4080 | Written notification to be given
-- src:4081 | 196 (1) The Attorney General of the province in which an application under subsection 185(1) was made or the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness if the application was made by or on behalf of that Minister shall, within 90 days after the period for which the authorization was given or renewed or within such other period as is fixed pursuant to subsection 185(3) or subsection (3) of this section, notify in writing the person who was the object of the interception pursuant to the authorization and shall, in a manner prescribed by regulations made by the Governor in Council, certify to the court that gave the authorization that the person has been so notified.
@ref Criminal Code s 196(1) (src:4080-4081)
GIVEN `the day the period for which the authorization was given or renewed ended` IS A DATE
      `the other period fixed pursuant to subsection 185(3) or 196(3)` IS A MAYBE `Length of time`
      `the number of days the running of the period was suspended under subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 196(1) the last day for notifying the person who was the object of the interception` MEANS
    (CONSIDER `the other period fixed pursuant to subsection 185(3) or 196(3)`
     WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the period for which the authorization was given or renewed ended` PLUS 90
     WHEN JUST other THEN `s 196(1) the day after a period that begins on the day` `the day the period for which the authorization was given or renewed ended` other)
    PLUS `the number of days the running of the period was suspended under subsection (2)`

-- src:4080 | Written notification to be given
-- src:4081 | 196 (1) The Attorney General of the province in which an application under subsection 185(1) was made or the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness if the application was made by or on behalf of that Minister shall, within 90 days after the period for which the authorization was given or renewed or within such other period as is fixed pursuant to subsection 185(3) or subsection (3) of this section, notify in writing the person who was the object of the interception pursuant to the authorization and shall, in a manner prescribed by regulations made by the Governor in Council, certify to the court that gave the authorization that the person has been so notified.
@ref Criminal Code s 196(1) (src:4080-4081)
GIVEN `the day the notice in writing was given` IS A DATE
      `s 196(1) the last day for notifying the person who was the object of the interception` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196(1) the notice was given in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice in writing was given` AT MOST `s 196(1) the last day for notifying the person who was the object of the interception`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, within 90 days after the period for which the authorization was given or renewed or within such other period as is fixed pursuant to subsection 185(3) or subsection (3) of this section, notify in writing"

DECLARE `s 196(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 196(1) notifies in writing the person who was the object of the interception`
    `s 196(1) certifies to the court that gave the authorization that the person has been notified`

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the clock starts the day the period for which the authorization was given or renewed ends (day 0); the notice is due within 90 days; once it is given the certificate follows (no period is stated for it).
-- src:4080 | Written notification to be given
-- src:4081 | 196 (1) The Attorney General of the province in which an application under subsection 185(1) was made or the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness if the application was made by or on behalf of that Minister shall, within 90 days after the period for which the authorization was given or renewed or within such other period as is fixed pursuant to subsection 185(3) or subsection (3) of this section, notify in writing the person who was the object of the interception pursuant to the authorization and shall, in a manner prescribed by regulations made by the Governor in Council, certify to the court that gave the authorization that the person has been so notified.
@ref Criminal Code s 196(1) (src:4080-4081)
GIVEN `the one bound` IS A `s 183 party under Part VI`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 183 party under Part VI` `s 196(1) act`
`s 196(1) the duty to notify the person and certify to the court as a rule` MEANS
    PARTY `the one bound`
    MUST `s 196(1) notifies in writing the person who was the object of the interception`
    WITHIN 90
    HENCE (PARTY `the one bound`
           MUST `s 196(1) certifies to the court that gave the authorization that the person has been notified`
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST BREACH BY `the one bound` BECAUSE "s 196(1): the person was notified but it was not certified to the court that gave the authorization")
    LEST BREACH BY `the one bound` BECAUSE "s 196(1): the person who was the object of the interception was not notified in writing within 90 days (or the other period fixed)"

-- 196(3): "Where the judge to whom an application referred to in subsection (2) is made, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, is satisfied that (a) the investigation of the offence to which the authorization relates, or (b) a subsequent
-- investigation of an offence listed in section 183 commenced as a result of information obtained from the investigation referred to in paragraph (a), is continuing and is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application,
-- the judge shall grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the period, each extension not to exceed three years."
-- src:4084 | Where extension to be granted
-- src:4085 | (3) Where the judge to whom an application referred to in subsection (2) is made, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, is satisfied that
-- src:4086 | (a) the investigation of the offence to which the authorization relates, or
-- src:4087 | (b) a subsequent investigation of an offence listed in section 183 commenced as a result of information obtained from the investigation referred to in paragraph (a),
-- src:4088 | is continuing and is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application, the judge shall grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the period, each extension not to exceed three years.
@ref Criminal Code s 196(3) (src:4084-4088)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the investigation of the offence to which the authorization relates is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that a subsequent investigation of an offence, commenced as a result of information obtained from that investigation, is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence of the subsequent investigation is listed in section 183, by s 183 offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is continuing and is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application"
        IF `the investigations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the investigations` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the judge to whom an application referred to in subsection (2) is made, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, is satisfied that"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the subsequent offence is "listed in section 183" is for that section and is not covered
    WHERE
        `the investigations` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued any of`
                (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the judge is satisfied that the investigation of the offence to which the authorization relates is continuing`
                    , `s 183 three-valued all of` (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the judge is satisfied that a subsequent investigation of an offence, commenced as a result of information obtained from that investigation, is continuing`, `the offence of the subsequent investigation is listed in section 183, by s 183 offence`))

-- src:4084 | Where extension to be granted
-- src:4085 | (3) Where the judge to whom an application referred to in subsection (2) is made, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, is satisfied that
-- src:4086 | (a) the investigation of the offence to which the authorization relates, or
-- src:4087 | (b) a subsequent investigation of an offence listed in section 183 commenced as a result of information obtained from the investigation referred to in paragraph (a),
-- src:4088 | is continuing and is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application, the judge shall grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the period, each extension not to exceed three years.
@ref Criminal Code s 196(3) (src:4084-4088)
GIVEN `the extension granted` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196(3) the extension is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `s 185(2) the period does not exceed three years` `the extension granted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each extension not to exceed three years"

-- 196(4): "An application pursuant to subsection (2) shall be accompanied by an affidavit deposing to (a) the facts known or believed by the deponent and relied on to justify the belief that an extension should be granted; and (b) the number of instances, if any,
-- on which an application has, to the knowledge or belief of the deponent, been made under that subsection in relation to the particular authorization and on which the application was withdrawn or the application was not granted, the date on which each
-- application was made and the judge to whom each application was made."
-- src:4089 | Application to be accompanied by affidavit
-- src:4090 | (4) An application pursuant to subsection (2) shall be accompanied by an affidavit deposing to
-- src:4091 | (a) the facts known or believed by the deponent and relied on to justify the belief that an extension should be granted; and
-- src:4092 | (b) the number of instances, if any, on which an application has, to the knowledge or belief of the deponent, been made under that subsection in relation to the particular authorization and on which the application was withdrawn or the application was not granted, the date on which each application was made and the judge to whom each application was made.
@ref Criminal Code s 196(4) (src:4089-4092)
GIVEN `the application is accompanied by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the facts known or believed by the deponent and relied on to justify the belief that an extension should be granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the number of instances on which an application under that subsection was withdrawn or not granted, the date of each and the judge to whom each was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196(4) the application meets the requirement of the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the application is accompanied by an affidavit` AND `the affidavit deposes to the facts known or believed by the deponent and relied on to justify the belief that an extension should be granted` AND `the affidavit deposes to the number of instances on which an application under that subsection was withdrawn or not granted, the date of each and the judge to whom each was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application pursuant to subsection (2) shall be accompanied by an affidavit deposing to"

-- 196(5): "Notwithstanding subsections (3) and 185(3), where the judge to whom an application referred to in subsection (2) or 185(2) is made, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, is satisfied that the investigation is in relation to
-- (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13, (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, or (c) a terrorism offence, and is of the opinion that the interests of
-- justice warrant the granting of the application, the judge shall grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the period, but no extension may exceed three years." This list has no limb for the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act (finding 3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:4093 | Exception for criminal organizations and terrorist groups
-- src:4094 | (5) Notwithstanding subsections (3) and 185(3), where the judge to whom an application referred to in subsection (2) or 185(2) is made, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, is satisfied that the investigation is in relation to
-- src:4095 | (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13,
-- src:4096 | (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, or
-- src:4097 | (c) a terrorism offence,
-- src:4098 | and is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application, the judge shall grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the period, but no extension may exceed three years.
@ref Criminal Code s 196(5) (src:4093-4098)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the investigation is in relation to the offence in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence the investigation is in relation to` IS A `s 183 provision of an Act`
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application"
        IF NOT `the judge is satisfied that the investigation is in relation to the offence in question`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is satisfied that the investigation is in relation to"
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is satisfied that the investigation is in relation to"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a criminal organization, or the offence a terrorism offence, is for another section and is not covered
    WHERE
        `the section` MEANS `the offence the investigation is in relation to`'s `section`
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            (`the offence the investigation is in relation to`'s `statute` EQUALS `s 183 the Criminal Code`)
            AND (`the section` EQUALS 52 OR `the section` EQUALS 52.1 OR `the section` EQUALS 52.2 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.11 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.111 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.12 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.13)
        `the limbs` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued any of`
                (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `limb (a)`
                    , `s 183 three-valued all of` (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group`, `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization`)
                    , `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`)

-- src:4093 | Exception for criminal organizations and terrorist groups
-- src:4094 | (5) Notwithstanding subsections (3) and 185(3), where the judge to whom an application referred to in subsection (2) or 185(2) is made, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, is satisfied that the investigation is in relation to
-- src:4095 | (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13,
-- src:4096 | (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, or
-- src:4097 | (c) a terrorism offence,
-- src:4098 | and is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application, the judge shall grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the period, but no extension may exceed three years.
@ref Criminal Code s 196(5) (src:4093-4098)
GIVEN `the extension granted` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196(5) the extension is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `s 185(2) the period does not exceed three years` `the extension granted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but no extension may exceed three years"

§ `Section 196.1 -- Written notice: interception in accordance with section 184.4`

-- 196.1(2): "The running of the 90-day period or of any extension granted under subsection (3) or (5) is suspended until any application made by the Attorney General of the province or the Minister to a judge ... for an extension or a subsequent extension of the
-- period has been heard and disposed of." The days of suspension are counted as in 196(2).
-- src:4101 | Extension of period for notification
-- src:4102 | (2) The running of the 90-day period or of any extension granted under subsection (3) or (5) is suspended until any application made by the Attorney General of the province or the Minister to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 for an extension or a subsequent extension of the period has been heard and disposed of.
@ref Criminal Code s 196.1(2) (src:4101-4102)
GIVEN `the day the application for an extension was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the application was heard and disposed of` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 196.1(2) the number of days the running of the period is suspended` MEANS
    IF Day `the day the application was heard and disposed of` AT LEAST Day `the day the application for an extension was made`
    THEN Day `the day the application was heard and disposed of` MINUS Day `the day the application for an extension was made`
    ELSE 0

-- 196.1(1): "Subject to subsections (3) and (5), the Attorney General of the province in which a police officer intercepts a private communication under section 184.4 or, if the interception relates to an offence for which proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General
-- of Canada, the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness shall give notice in writing of the interception to any person who was the object of the interception within 90 days after the day on which it occurred."
-- The last day for the notice: the day of the interception plus 90 days, plus any extension granted under (3) or (5) (FORK F15: the text caps "each extension" at three years; whether the extension is added to the 90 days or replaces them is not said, and it is added here), plus the days the running was suspended by (2).
-- src:4099 | Written notice — interception in accordance with section 184.4
-- src:4100 | 196.1 (1) Subject to subsections (3) and (5), the Attorney General of the province in which a police officer intercepts a private communication under section 184.4 or, if the interception relates to an offence for which proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General of Canada, the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness shall give notice in writing of the interception to any person who was the object of the interception within 90 days after the day on which it occurred.
@ref Criminal Code s 196.1(1) (src:4099-4100)
GIVEN `the day on which the interception occurred` IS A DATE
      `the extension granted under subsection (3) or (5)` IS A MAYBE `Length of time`
      `the number of days the running of the period was suspended under subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 196.1(1) the last day for giving notice of the interception` MEANS
    (CONSIDER `the extension granted under subsection (3) or (5)`
     WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day on which the interception occurred` PLUS 90
     WHEN JUST extension THEN `s 196(1) the day after a period that begins on the day` (`the day on which the interception occurred` PLUS 90) extension)
    PLUS `the number of days the running of the period was suspended under subsection (2)`

-- src:4099 | Written notice — interception in accordance with section 184.4
-- src:4100 | 196.1 (1) Subject to subsections (3) and (5), the Attorney General of the province in which a police officer intercepts a private communication under section 184.4 or, if the interception relates to an offence for which proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General of Canada, the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness shall give notice in writing of the interception to any person who was the object of the interception within 90 days after the day on which it occurred.
@ref Criminal Code s 196.1(1) (src:4099-4100)
GIVEN `the day the notice in writing was given` IS A DATE
      `s 196.1(1) the last day for giving notice of the interception` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196.1(1) the notice was given in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice in writing was given` AT MOST `s 196.1(1) the last day for giving notice of the interception`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall give notice in writing of the interception to any person who was the object of the interception within 90 days after the day on which it occurred"

DECLARE `s 196.1(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 196.1(1) gives notice in writing of the interception to the person who was the object of it`

-- src:4099 | Written notice — interception in accordance with section 184.4
-- src:4100 | 196.1 (1) Subject to subsections (3) and (5), the Attorney General of the province in which a police officer intercepts a private communication under section 184.4 or, if the interception relates to an offence for which proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General of Canada, the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness shall give notice in writing of the interception to any person who was the object of the interception within 90 days after the day on which it occurred.
@ref Criminal Code s 196.1(1) (src:4099-4100)
GIVEN `the one bound` IS A `s 183 party under Part VI`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 183 party under Part VI` `s 196.1(1) act`
`s 196.1(1) the duty to give notice of the interception as a rule` MEANS
    PARTY `the one bound`
    MUST `s 196.1(1) gives notice in writing of the interception to the person who was the object of it`
    WITHIN 90
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the one bound` BECAUSE "s 196.1(1): notice in writing of the interception was not given to the person who was the object of it within 90 days"

-- 196.1(3): "The judge to whom an application under subsection (2) is made shall grant an extension or a subsequent extension of the 90-day period — each extension not to exceed three years — if the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant
-- granting the application and is satisfied, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, that one of the following investigations is continuing: (a) the investigation of the offence to which the interception relates; or (b) a subsequent
-- investigation of an offence commenced as a result of information obtained from the investigation referred to in paragraph (a)." (Unlike 196(3)(b), no listing in section 183 is required.)
-- src:4103 | Where extension to be granted
-- src:4104 | (3) The judge to whom an application under subsection (2) is made shall grant an extension or a subsequent extension of the 90-day period — each extension not to exceed three years — if the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application and is satisfied, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, that one of the following investigations is continuing:
-- src:4105 | (a) the investigation of the offence to which the interception relates; or
-- src:4106 | (b) a subsequent investigation of an offence commenced as a result of information obtained from the investigation referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref Criminal Code s 196.1(3) (src:4103-4106)
GIVEN `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the investigation of the offence to which the interception relates is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that a subsequent investigation of an offence commenced as a result of information obtained from that investigation is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196.1(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` MEANS
    IF `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application` AND (`the judge is satisfied that the investigation of the offence to which the interception relates is continuing` OR `the judge is satisfied that a subsequent investigation of an offence commenced as a result of information obtained from that investigation is continuing`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application and is satisfied, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, that one of the following investigations is continuing"

-- src:4103 | Where extension to be granted
-- src:4104 | (3) The judge to whom an application under subsection (2) is made shall grant an extension or a subsequent extension of the 90-day period — each extension not to exceed three years — if the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application and is satisfied, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, that one of the following investigations is continuing:
-- src:4105 | (a) the investigation of the offence to which the interception relates; or
-- src:4106 | (b) a subsequent investigation of an offence commenced as a result of information obtained from the investigation referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref Criminal Code s 196.1(3) (src:4103-4106)
GIVEN `the extension granted` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196.1(3) the extension is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `s 185(2) the period does not exceed three years` `the extension granted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each extension not to exceed three years"

-- 196.1(4): "An application shall be accompanied by an affidavit deposing to (a) the facts known or believed by the deponent and relied on to justify the belief that an extension should be granted; and (b) the number of instances, if any, ... in relation to the
-- particular interception and on which the application was withdrawn or the application was not granted, the date on which each application was made and the judge to whom each application was made."
-- src:4107 | Application to be accompanied by affidavit
-- src:4108 | (4) An application shall be accompanied by an affidavit deposing to
-- src:4109 | (a) the facts known or believed by the deponent and relied on to justify the belief that an extension should be granted; and
-- src:4110 | (b) the number of instances, if any, on which an application has, to the knowledge or belief of the deponent, been made under subsection (2) in relation to the particular interception and on which the application was withdrawn or the application was not granted, the date on which each application was made and the judge to whom each application was made.
@ref Criminal Code s 196.1(4) (src:4107-4110)
GIVEN `the application is accompanied by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the facts known or believed by the deponent and relied on to justify the belief that an extension should be granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the number of instances on which an application under subsection (2) was withdrawn or not granted, the date of each and the judge to whom each was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196.1(4) the application meets the requirement of the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the application is accompanied by an affidavit` AND `the affidavit deposes to the facts known or believed by the deponent and relied on to justify the belief that an extension should be granted` AND `the affidavit deposes to the number of instances on which an application under subsection (2) was withdrawn or not granted, the date of each and the judge to whom each was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application shall be accompanied by an affidavit deposing to"

-- 196.1(5): "Despite subsection (3), the judge to whom an application under subsection (2) is made shall grant an extension or a subsequent extension of the 90-day period — each extension not to exceed three years — if the judge is of the opinion that the interests
-- of justice warrant granting the application and is satisfied, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, that the interception of the communication relates to an investigation of (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.12 or 467.13;
-- (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization; (b.1) an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or (c) a terrorism offence."
-- This list names 467.11, 467.12 and 467.13 and not 467.111, which 185(1.1)(a), 186(1.1)(a), 186.1(a) and 196(5)(a) name (finding 3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:4111 | Exception — criminal organization or terrorism offence
-- src:4112 | (5) Despite subsection (3), the judge to whom an application under subsection (2) is made shall grant an extension or a subsequent extension of the 90-day period — each extension not to exceed three years — if the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application and is satisfied, on the basis of an affidavit submitted in support of the application, that the interception of the communication relates to an investigation of
-- src:4113 | (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.12 or 467.13;
-- src:4114 | (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization;
-- src:4115 | (b.1) an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or
-- src:4116 | (c) a terrorism offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 196.1(5) (src:4111-4116)
GIVEN `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the interception of the communication relates to an investigation of the offence in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence the investigation is of` IS A `s 183 provision of an Act`
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application"
        IF NOT `the judge is satisfied that the interception of the communication relates to an investigation of the offence in question`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that the interception of the communication relates to an investigation of"
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that the interception of the communication relates to an investigation of"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a criminal organization, or the offence a terrorism offence, is for another section and is not covered
    WHERE
        `the section` MEANS `the offence the investigation is of`'s `section`
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            (`the offence the investigation is of`'s `statute` EQUALS `s 183 the Criminal Code`)
            AND (`the section` EQUALS 52 OR `the section` EQUALS 52.1 OR `the section` EQUALS 52.2 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.11 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.12 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.13)
        `limb (b.1)` MEANS
            (`the offence the investigation is of`'s `statute` EQUALS `s 183 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`)
            AND (`the offence the investigation is of`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            AND (`the section` EQUALS 20 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.1 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.2 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.3 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.4)
        `the limbs` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued any of`
                (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `limb (a)`
                    , `s 183 three-valued all of` (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group`, `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization`)
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `limb (b.1)`
                    , `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`)

